  "text_md": "26 KE FENG, HUABIN GE, YUNPENG MENG\n\nRecall the functions cov(l) and H(l) are defined in (4.3 and 4.4) respectively. For the sake of subsequent elaboration, we rewrite the functions cov and H as\n\n# (5.3) covh(lh) = cov(l∗,lh) = cov(l) =\n\nand\n\ncovσ(lσh) +\n\ncovσ(lσ)\n\nσ∈T3,1\n\nσ∈T4,0\n\n# (5.4) Hh(lh) = H(l∗,lh) = H(l) = cov(l) − 2π\n\nli,\n\ni∈E\n\nwhere T3,1 (T4,0, resp.) represents the set of 3-1 type (4-0 type, resp.) tetrahedra in T . Lemma 5.3. For (M,T ), let lh ∈ Lh(M,T ) be a hyper-ideal edge length vector, then\n\n∂Hh ∂li\n\n= −Ki, ei ∈ Eh.\n\nProof. For any ei ∈ Eh, if the hyper-ideal edge ei is not a side of any 3-1 type tetrahedron in T , then (4-1) in [9] had proved the conclusion. On the contrary, ei is a side of some 3-1 type hyperbolic tetrahedra, take such a 3-1 tetrahedron (σ,lσ), with\n\nlσ = (l12(l23,l24,l34),l13(l23,l24,l34),l14(l23,l24,l34),l23,l24,l34), where (l23,l24,l34) = lσh ∈ R3, then\n\n∂ covσ(lσh) ∂l23\n\n∂cov(lσ) ∂l23\n\n=\n\n∂cov ∂l23\n\n∂cov ∂l12\n\n∂l12 ∂l23\n\n∂cov ∂l13\n\n∂l13 ∂l23\n\n∂cov ∂l14\n\n∂l14 ∂l23\n\n- (5.5)\n\n= α23 + α12\n\n∂l12 ∂l23\n\n+ α13\n\n∂l13 ∂l23\n\n+ α14\n\n∂l14 ∂l23\n\n= α23 +\n\nπ 3\n\n∂ ∂l23\n\nl12 + l13 + l14 . Similarly, we also have\n\n- (5.6)\n\n∂ covσ(lσh) ∂l24\n\n= α24 +\n\nπ 3\n\n∂ ∂l24\n\nl12 + l13 + l14 . and\n\n- (5.7)\n\n\n=\n\n+\n\n+\n\n+\n\n∂ covσ(lσh) ∂l34\n\n∂ ∂l34\n\nπ 3\n\n= α34 +\n\nl12 + l13 + l14 .\n\nSubstitute (5.5), (5.6) and (5.7) into the following calculation of ∂Hh/∂li, we have\n\n",
